^^

What this means:
  Before a parameter's type or `self`:
    `name: ^^T` says the function takes that argument for good; `^^self` takes the receiver.
    Example:
      archive: fn(name: ^^String) -> String { name }
      saved: archive(title)
    Afterwards: The call is written plain. The caller's value moves into the function, and a later use is the error Jet.MoveWithoutMarker, which names the call. To keep using it, pass `title.copy()`.
    Related: Jet.MoveWithoutMarker

  After `task`, before a name:
    `task ^^name { … }` moves one enclosing value into the task.
    Example:
      job: Job{id: 7}
      task ^^job { job.run() }
    Afterwards: The task owns the value; a later use of the name is the error Jet.UseAfterMove.
    Related: Jet.UseAfterMove

This explanation comes from Jet's syntax dictionary.

Registry name: SIGIL_MOVE
